l purposes">The seeds of this plant are dark red and are commonly used in cooking and for medicinal purposes</span>. <span class ="tr_" id="tr_37" data-source="" data-orig="In traditional Chinese medicine">In traditional Chinese medicine</span>, <span class ="tr_" id="tr_38" data-source="" data-orig="red beans are used to treat symptoms such as damp-heat accumulation">red beans are used to treat symptoms such as damp-heat accumulation</span>, <span class ="tr_" id="tr_39" data-source="" data-orig="hematuria">hematuria</span>, <span class ="tr_" id="tr_40" data-source="" data-orig="and abdominal edema">and abdominal edema</span>, <span class ="tr_" id="tr_41" data-source="" data-orig="and they can serve as a high-protein">and they can serve as a high-protein</span>, <span class ="tr_" id="tr_42" data-source="" data-orig="low-calorie food">low-calorie food</span>.</p><h2><span class="ez-toc-section" id="What_are_Kidney_Beans"></span><strong><span class ="tr_" id="tr_43" data-source="" data-orig="What are Kidney Beans">What are Kidney Beans</span>?</strong><span class="ez-toc-section-end"></span></h2><p><span class ="tr_" id="tr_44" data-source="" data-orig="Kidney beans">Kidney beans</span>, <span class ="tr_" id="tr_45" data-source="" data-orig="scientifically known as Phaseolus vulgaris L.">scientifically known as Phaseolus vulgaris L.</span>, <span class ="tr_" id="tr_46" data-source="" data-orig="are also legumes">are also legumes</span>, <span class ="tr_" id="tr_47" data-source="" data-orig="commonly referred to as common beans">commonly referred to as common beans</span>, <span class ="tr_" id="tr_48" data-source="" data-orig="snap beans">snap beans</span>, <span class ="tr_" id="tr_49" data-source="" data-orig="or pole beans">or pole beans</span>. <span class ="tr_" id="tr_50" data-source="" data-orig="They are annual">They are annual</span>, <span class ="tr_" id="tr_51" data-source="" data-orig="climbing or nearly erect herbs with flowers that can be white">climbing or nearly erect herbs with flowers that can be white</span>, <span class ="tr_" id="tr_52" data-source="" data-orig="yellow">yellow</span>, <span class ="tr_" id="tr_53" data-source="" data-orig="light purple">light purple</span>, <span class ="tr_" id="tr_54" data-source="" data-orig="or purple">or purple</span>. In China, <span class ="tr_" id="tr_55" data-source="" data-orig="kidney beans have been cultivated since the Tang Dynasty">kidney beans have been cultivated since the Tang Dynasty</span>. <span class ="tr_" id="tr_56" data-source="" data-orig="They are suitable for planting in temperate and tropical high-altitude areas">They are suitable for planting in temperate and tropical high-altitude areas</span>, <span class ="tr_" id="tr_57" data-source="" data-orig="showing a good tolerance for cold and a preference for sunlight">showing a good tolerance for cold and a preference for sunlight</span>. <span class ="tr_" id="tr_58" data-source="" data-orig="Kidney beans are high in potassium and magnesium">Kidney beans are high in potassium and magnesium</span>, <span class ="tr_" id="tr_59" data-source="" data-orig="low in sodium">low in sodium</span>, <span class ="tr_" id="tr_60" data-source="" data-orig="and rich in protein">and rich in protein</span>, Ballaststoffe, Aminosäuren, <span class ="tr_" id="tr_61" data-source="" data-orig="and minerals like iron">and minerals like iron</span>. <span class ="tr_" id="tr_62" data-source="" data-orig="Research on low-sugar kidney bean preserves indicates they can boost immunity and are beneficial for skin and hair health">Research on low-sugar kidney bean preserves indicates they can boost immunity and are beneficial for skin and hair health</span>.</p><h2><span class="ez-toc-section" id="Are_Red_Beans_and_Red_Kidney_Beans_the_Same_What_are_the_Differences_How_to_Distinguish_Them"></span><strong><span class ="tr_" id="tr_63" data-source="" data-orig="Are Red Beans and Red Kidney Beans the Same">Are Red Beans and Red Kidney Beans the Same</span>? <span class ="tr_" id="tr_64" data-source="" data-orig="What are the Differences">What are the Differences</span>? <span class ="tr_" id="tr_65" data-source="" data-orig="How to Distinguish Them">How to Distinguish Them</span>?</strong><span class="ez-toc-section-end"></span></h2><p><span class ="tr_" id="tr_66" data-source="" data-orig="Although both are red">Although both are red</span>, <span class ="tr_" id="tr_67" data-source="" data-orig="they are not the same">they are not the same</span>. <span class ="tr_" id="tr_68" data-source="" data-orig="They have distinct differences in appearance">They have distinct differences in appearance</span>, <span class ="tr_" id="tr_69" data-source="" data-orig="nutritional content">nutritional content</span>, Herkunft, <span class ="tr_" id="tr_70" data-source="" data-orig="and taste">and taste</span>.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><table style="border: 2px solid black; border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%;"><tbody><tr><th style="border: 1px solid black; padding: 8px; background-color: #f2f2f2;"><span class ="tr_" id="tr_71" data-source="" data-orig="Variety">Variety</span></th><th style="border: 1px solid black; padding: 8px; background-color: #f2f2f2;">Aussehen</th><th style="border: 1px solid black; padding: 8px; background-color: #f2f2f2;">Nährstoffgehalt</th><th style="border: 1px solid black; padding: 8px; background-color: #f2f2f2;">Herkunft</th><th style="border: 1px solid black; padding: 8px; background-color: #f2f2f2;">Schmecken</th></tr><tr><td style="border: 1px solid black; padding: 8px;">Rote Bohnen</td><td style="border: 1px solid black; padding: 8px;">Kleiner, <span class ="tr_" id="tr_72" data-source="" data-orig="usually oval-shaped">usually oval-shaped</span>, <span class ="tr_" id="tr_73" data-source="" data-orig="dark red or purple">dark red or purple</span>.</td><td style="border: 1px solid black; padding: 8px;"><span class ="tr_" id="tr_74" data-source="" data-orig="High in protein">High in protein</span>, <span class ="tr_" id="tr_75" data-source="" data-orig="contains essential amino acids">contains essential amino acids</span>.</td><td style="border: 1px solid black; padding: 8px;"><span class ="tr_" id="tr_76" data-source="" data-orig="Grown in southern and northern China">Grown in southern and northern China</span>, <span class ="tr_" id="tr_77" data-source="" data-orig="Congo">Congo</span>, <span class ="tr_" id="tr_78" data-source="" data-orig="and Uganda">and Uganda</span>.</td><td style="border: 1px solid black; padding: 8px;"><span class ="tr_" id="tr_79" data-source="" data-orig="Slightly sweet">Slightly sweet</span></td></tr><tr><td style="border: 1px solid black; padding: 8px;"><span class ="tr_" id="tr_80" data-source="" data-orig="Red Kidney Beans">Red Kidney Beans</span></td><td style="border: 1px solid black; padding: 8px;"><span class ="tr_" id="tr_81" data-source="" data-orig="Larger and kidney-shaped">Larger and kidney-shaped</span>, <span class ="tr_" id="tr_82" data-source="" data-orig="bright red">bright red</span>.</td><td style="border: 1px solid black; padding: 8px;"><span class ="tr_" id="tr_83" data-source="" data-orig="Rich in vitamins">Rich in vitamins</span>, Ballaststoffe, Kalzium, Eisen, <span class ="tr_" id="tr_84" data-source="" data-orig="and zinc">and zinc</span>.</td><td style="border: 1px solid black; padding: 8px;"><span class ="tr_" id="tr_85" data-source="" data-orig="Mainly produced in Shanxi">Mainly produced in Shanxi</span>, China.</td><td style="border: 1px solid black; padding: 8px;"><span class ="tr_" id="tr_86" data-source="" data-orig="Richer flavor">Richer flavor</span></td></tr></tbody></table><h2><span class="ez-toc-section" id="_What_Foods_are_made_from_Red_Beans_and_Kidney_Beans"></span> <strong><span class ="tr_" id="tr_87" data-source="" data-orig="What Foods are made from Red Beans and Kidney Beans">What Foods are made from Red Beans and Kidney Beans</span>?</strong><span class="